 both at $p=6$. Independent coarse direct solves give matching errors.}
 \label{tab:adr-stress-accuracy}
\end{table}

Separate CUDA-event profiles of the anisotropic case give mean complete
ASM+PP application times of 1.063 and 4.495~ms on the coarse and fine meshes
(ten samples after three warmups). Preconditioning accounts for 83.2\% and
90.5\% of attributed GPU operation time. These instrumented measurements do
not enter the solver ranking; overlapping host synchronization waits must not
be added to GPU times. The completed $p$MG--AMG measurements separate setup and reuse below.

